# openWallet code owners.
#
# The floor is narrow on purpose, as openXwallet's is: what decides WHICH commit
# of each leg this project is, the checks that hold those to their pins, the
# release identity that names both legs, and the workflows that decide whether
# the checks run at all. A pull request that could change what runs cannot
# clear itself.

# The leg gitlinks. Each moves only with its pin, in one commit.
/spec   @brettheap
/code   @brettheap

# Where each leg is fetched from.
/.gitmodules   @brettheap

# The manifest that says what this project IS.
/project.yaml   @brettheap

# The pins (spec, code, shape) and the naming policy. From the carve onward,
# this also covers the release identity: contracts/manifest.yaml,
# contracts/CHANGELOG.md and contracts/releases/.
/contracts/   @brettheap

# The shape's validators and bootstrap, copied from openRepoShape and
# digest-pinned in contracts/shape-pin.yaml.
/scripts/   @brettheap

# Whether the checks run, in what order, and under which status-check token.
/.github/workflows/   @brettheap
